# Layout components

Do **not** use `c-layout`. It is a legacy compatibility component and must not be added to new or migrated code.

Use Vuetify's `v-row` and `v-col` components for grid layouts. For simple flex layouts, use Vuetify flex utility classes such as `d-flex`, `flex-column`, `align-center`, and `justify-space-between` on a native element.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<c-layout align="center" justify="space-between">
  <!-- content -->
</c-layout>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: grid layout -->
<v-row align="center" justify="space-between">
  <!-- content -->
</v-row>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: simple flex layout -->
<div class="d-flex align-center justify-space-between">
  <!-- content -->
</div>
```
